# The sandbar release that drives this repo's own unattended series (#66).
#
# `npm run sandbar` installs exactly this into `.sandbar/driver/` and runs it.
# Nothing after that point is built from the working tree, so an operator can
# hold local commits and uncommitted edits while a series runs.
#
# One npm spec, `github:<owner>/<repo>#v<major>.<minor>.<patch>`. A TAG, as a
# consumer would pin: an untagged state is not pinnable and a sha is not a
# substitute for one. The tag for a version is created by `auto-tag.yml` on the
# push to `main` that lands it, so a pin only becomes installable once its
# version is on `main`.
#
# `auto-tag.yml` tags the version at the PUSHED HEAD, and the merger lands a
# whole source pass in one push, so a version that is not the last one in a pass
# never gets a tag. A pin naming such a version is uninstallable for good, and
# the launcher stops the loop saying exactly that rather than running something
# else — which is the design, but it makes "the pin names a version that never
# became a tag" a real state. The fix is one commit, and it is TWO edits when
# the fallback is an older release: move the line below to a version
# `git tag --list 'v*'` actually shows, and lower `requiresSandbar` in
# `sandbar.config.mjs` to something that release satisfies — otherwise the
# driver installs and then refuses the config it was installed to read. No
# backfill; an untagged state is simply not pinnable.
#
# Moving it is a one-line commit, made deliberately after watching a version
# behave — that delay IS the feature. Iterating unlanded orchestrator code stays
# a `npm run build && node dist/cli.js` away, by hand.
#
# Lines starting with `#` are comments; exactly one spec line must remain.
github:Tojins/sandbar#v0.21.2
